---
description: Apply the shared Issue, ownership, integration and GUI lease contract to repository changes, even without an explicit Git request
alwaysApply: true
---

Apply [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and the [GitHub workflow](../../docs/development/github-workflow.md#参照する範囲と進行判断) to changes. Use their conditional reference table before design: Mission/ACP First for new features/integration, relevant requirements/design for product changes, corresponding policies for operational work. Do not generalize print observations to every transport or treat unimplemented ACP/unobserved GUI as complete. Additional agents follow the [Codex execution policy](../../docs/development/codex-execution-policy.md).

Use [start-work](../../.agents/skills/start-work/SKILL.md) for Issue/claim → dedicated Issue branch/worktree → Draft PR, and [finish-work](../../.agents/skills/finish-work/SKILL.md) for tests/independent review → integration/QA/cleanup. One writer per task/worktree; record state/handoffs in the Issue. No direct main/develop commits/pushes. The shared contract retains develop tracking versus full fixed-candidate main acceptance, bidirectional QA readback before implementation closure, and protection of main/develop, existing owners and PAUSED heartbeat. Stop the writer before clean v2 opaque enrollment; the coordinator owns later fixes/review/merge/Issue updates/branch cleanup. Keep host/source in the private registry and never concurrently edit an enrolled branch.

Cursor can own product implementation, documentation or configuration under the same [role conditions](../../docs/development/github-workflow.md#正本と役割) as other development agents. Choose roles by available tools, authorization and ownership; fixture-only limits apply to product test inputs, not to the development client. GUI operations, runIde, installation and restart require the [host-wide lease](../../docs/development/gui-coordination.md); separate worktrees do not permit simultaneous GUI operation. Do not use stale builds/screens/expired reservations. Other tasks may continue implementation/tests/review while GUI waits; retain unverified states in the Issue.

For new or updated development context and context reviews/audits, apply the [single context policy](../../docs/architecture/knowledge.md#開発コンテキストの用途言語形式と読込条件). Do not create client-specific copies of it. Human-facing outputs remain Japanese.
